import Mathlib

/-!
# GlobalShtukasAndFunctionFieldLanglands: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It records which headline theorems
can be stated against the pinned Mathlib and Tau Ceti APIs.

The headline theorems are geometric Satake (rational, integral and arithmetic), the geometry
and compactly supported cohomology of global shtukas, the integral Eichler–Shimura relation,
Drinfeld descent and ind-smoothness for shtuka cohomology, the PGL₂ Eisenstein decomposition,
the global cuspidal excursion decomposition with its nonsplit and modular forms, companions
on curves, and the local parameterization with local–global compatibility and gamma factors.

None is statable on its actual carriers at these pins. Satake lacks the affine and
Beilinson–Drinfeld Grassmannians, the perverse étale-sheaf categories on them with convolution,
and the total-cohomology fibre functor; its representation side is present, since Tau Ceti
supplies finite algebraic representations of an affine group through
`TauCeti.FGPointRepresentationCat` and its comodule equivalence
`TauCeti.fgPointRepresentationCategoryEquivalence`. Shtuka geometry,
Eichler–Shimura and the Eisenstein theorem lack algebraic moduli stacks and their ℓ-adic
cohomology. Drinfeld descent and ind-smoothness lack lisse and constructible étale coefficient
categories and Frobenius–Weil actions on that cohomology. The global excursion theorem lacks
the fixed-level automorphic cusp space and its geometric operators. Companions lack lisse
ℓ-adic sheaves on curves. The local theorem lacks smooth admissible representation categories,
the completed Bernstein centre and the Weil–Deligne comparison. The bundle-mass and function-field SL_r volume theorems
lack the completed function-field adelic groups with their Haar and gauge measures; the
elliptic-sheaf comparison lacks the periodic bundle-chain moduli carrier. The elementary numerical
and abstract algebraic API in README.md does not replace these headlines.
-/

